' 4+1 process view - Request a new password (US05) · no enumeration, per-account limit, token made at send time
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: The response is always the same, at most one message per account and interval, and the token is made by the worker at send time (US05).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-reset-request
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - request a new password (US05): no enumeration, per-account limit, token made at send time
autonumber

participant "Accounts" as WEB_F_AUTH
box "ASP.NET Core API"
  participant "Accounts and sessions" as API_AUTH
  participant "Recovery" as API_AUTH_RESET
  participant "Process the outbox" as API_NOTIF_PROC
  participant "Data Protection" as CC_DATAPROT
  participant "Send" as API_NOTIF_SENDER
end box
database "PostgreSQL" as C_DB
participant "SMTP server" as X_SMTP <<external>>

== On the request ==
WEB_F_AUTH -> API_AUTH : POST /api/auth/password-reset/request { email }\n[[AllowAnonymous], per-IP limit]
API_AUTH -> API_AUTH_RESET : RequestAsync: validates the format (400 only for a malformed email)
API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : QueueResetEmailAsync: FindByEmailAsync and profiles [SELECT users,\nuser_roles]
alt no account, deactivated, or Admin
  API_AUTH_RESET -> API_AUTH_RESET : Does nothing
else active Player or Owner
  group Transaction
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : SELECT 1 FROM users WHERE id = … FOR UPDATE (one request at a\ntime per account) [SQL]
    API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : max(created_at) of this account's password_reset messages [SELECT\noutbox_messages]
    alt there is one less than 5 min old
      API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : ROLLBACK, silently [SQL]
    else
      API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : INSERT outbox_messages (password_reset, { accountId }), without a\ntoken; COMMIT [SQL]
    end
  end
end
API_AUTH --> WEB_F_AUTH : 202 PasswordResetRequested.Always: the same response in every\ncase

== Later, in the worker ==
API_NOTIF_PROC -> C_DB : Claims the message (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) [SQL]
API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_AUTH_RESET : AccountEmailBuilder.BuildAsync(password_reset, payload)
API_AUTH_RESET -> C_DB : FindByIdAsync; checks again that the account is eligible (otherwise null →\nrecipient_not_found) [SELECT users]
API_AUTH_RESET -> CC_DATAPROT : GeneratePasswordResetTokenAsync(user)
CC_DATAPROT -> C_DB : Data Protection keys [SELECT data_protection_keys]
CC_DATAPROT --> API_AUTH_RESET : Token with the security stamp; valid for 1 h by the system clock
API_AUTH_RESET -> API_AUTH_RESET : PasswordResetRules.Link(PublicSite:BaseUrl, email, token);\nAccountEmailComposer.PasswordReset
API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_SENDER : SendAsync(email)
API_NOTIF_SENDER -> X_SMTP : Sends; the token exists only in this email [SMTP]
@enduml
